<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Act of Independence of Lithuania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · Also known as Act of 16 February</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Act of Independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> was signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> on 16 February 1918 by the twenty members of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-lithuania">Council of Lithuania</a>, chaired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanas-smetona">Antanas Smetona</a>. It proclaimed an independent, democratic Lithuanian state with Vilnius as its capital, severing all earlier ties with other nations. Although German troops still occupied the country, the date is celebrated as Lithuania's State Restoration Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/act-of-independence-of-lithuania.jpg" alt="Act of Independence of Lithuania" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Council of Lithuania · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Original_Act_of_Independence_of_Lithuania_hand-written_in_Lithuanian_language.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
